FEE EXPLANATION (reusable support snippet)

Brokerage & trade charges - what to know
- Brokerage is the fee the broker charges for each executed equity order; Gro=
ww publishes its current rates on its pricing page.
- Brokerage is not the only cost: statutory charges such as STT, exchange tra=
nsaction charges, GST, SEBI turnover fees and stamp duty are added by regulat=
ion and are not set by the broker.
- Selling delivery shares also attracts depository (DP) charges, applied per =
stock sold per day.
- Charges apply per executed order, so splitting one trade into several order=
s can increase the total fee.
- Every charge is itemised in the contract note and ledger for each trade.
- Net profit on a trade equals gross profit minus brokerage and all statutory=
 and DP charges.

Sources: Groww pricing and charges (https://groww.in/pricing) | Groww Help Ce=
